Add a max_topk 2048 tier to DeepSelect's BF16 top-k (csrc/api.cpp) for
1024 < topk <= 2048, the DSA sparse indexer's prefill top-k. Applied by
cmake/external_projects/deepselect.cmake to the pinned DeepSelect checkout.

- That range used the max_topk 4096 tuple (512 threads, occupancy 1,
  B 8192, B2 4096, TMA depth 3). The new tier is the same tuple with
  max_topk 2048: the scan order, the segment permutation, the reconstruct
  threshold and the tie handling do not depend on max_topk, which only sizes
  the candidate buffers and the loops over them.
- Output indices (and their order) are identical to the max_topk 4096 tuple.
- Adds the eight bf16 instantiations of the new tuple and lets the bf16
  normal kernel accept max_topk 2048.

diff --git a/csrc/api.cpp b/csrc/api.cpp
index c6e238f..b1f1593 100644
--- a/csrc/api.cpp
+++ b/csrc/api.cpp
@@ -174,6 +174,10 @@ void topk(
                             dispatch.template operator()<512>();
                         } else if (topk <= 1024) {
                             dispatch.template operator()<1024>();
+                        } else if (topk <= 2048) {
+                            // Modified by NVIDIA: topk in (1024, 2048] uses the same tuple as the big-topk tier
+                            // (512t / occ1 / B8192 / B2 4096 / TMA3) with max_topk 2048 (smaller buffers, same scan order).
+                            topk_select_bf16_normal::run_topk_select_kernel<TopkSelectConfig<nv_bfloat16, OutIdxT, false, SORTED_INDEX, RETURN_VALUE, 2048, 512, 1, 8192, 4096, 3>>(args);
                         } else {
                             // Big-topk coverage tier, topk in (1024, 4096]: one correctness-only tuple
                             // (512t / occ1 / B8192 / B2 4096 / TMA3 / max_topk 4096), no wave split.
